Total Appropriated by Fund:
WATER DEVELOPMENT I $534,998
WATER DEVELOPMENT II $980,000
WATER DEVELOPMENT III $551,000
Description of appropriation:
The 900 series expenditures will be used for contract services to complete Level
I Reconnaissance Studies and Level II Feasibility Studies for New Development,
Rehabilitation and Dam Reservoir Projects.
The 600 series expenditures will be used for a grant to the University of Wyoming
to administer and conduct water research. These funds are augmented with those
from the United States Geological Survey and the University of Wyoming.
This bill is effective immediately. As reflected above, it is anticipated that a
total of $402,938 will be expended before July 1, 2025 ($372,318 from Water
Development Account I, $19,600 from Water Development Account II, and $11,020
from Water Development Account III).
